{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "scope": "conditional decoded specification property only",
  "boundaries": {
    "context": "HistoricalContext derives origin, latest-at-cutoff registry entries and covered anchor lookups from typed authenticated inputs. RegistryHistory models lifetime identities and entry checkpoints; actual root/key-byte validation, genesis provenance and complete evidence/token accounting remain external.",
    "l1": "Real raw-header ancestry, canonicality/finality, storage/MPT parsing and authentication are external.",
    "signature": "The signature relation authenticates decoded vote fields and key; actual low-s/ecrecover/sign-byte encoding is external. Full Comet lock/round safety is not derived here.",
    "payload": "Envelope/tx0/raw/singleton bindings and full-range blob-to-payload equality are external named relations, not actual guest proofs.",
    "el": "Complete deterministic EL execution, header/body fields and zk-gas semantics remain external relations.",
    "hash": "Opaque/free hash terms, actual cryptographic separation and canonical encodings remain external.",
    "journal": "ProtocolState composes decoded landing/registry/FI/recovery/rollback transactions under nondecreasing L1 time and structural initial invariants. EVM atomicity, trusted rollback target/snapshot, DAO cancellation of outstanding authorizations and node trust remain external; irreversible payouts are not restored.",
    "deployment": "Stored initialized L, genesisCutoff, K, maxAnchorAge and forcedInclusionDelay, the committee-0 and config commitments, and their authenticated ghost openings: the 4-field config opening (vp_unit, s_min, n_max, U), which the config commitment hashes as seven ABI words together with the domain tag, l2ChainId and registry, and the committee-0 record; plus the World's fixed hash adapters. Every modeled transition preserves them and no transaction input chooses them. Opening authentication and real hash/preimage separation are explicit external assumptions (the representable_opening_unique premise; Premises.hashSeparation for the deployment's own commitment), not proven by a free Rules field."
  },
